                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a969cd9-2422-43a4-b3cb-2fb1436ad76c",
                                "sense_id": "ce629df0-42a0-30ee-9267-482ce60b7acf",
                                "text": "Most final consonants have been lost, resulting in a tonal language with a rich consonantal and vocalic inventory, but with a relatively simple syllabic structure.."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98849396-b198-3153-ac78-ab8ca443b8ed",
                        "entry_id": "788443b2-9511-3df3-87f8-a335766be8f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pronounced with every syllable distinct."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "88b3b24b-8164-347f-9f68-fd187b21c85b",
                        "entry_id": "788443b2-9511-3df3-87f8-a335766be8f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Designating a sound that is or can be the most sonorant segment of a syllable, as a vowel or a resonant. In the word riddle ([ɹɪdl̩]), the two syllabic sounds are [ɪ] and [l̩]."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a9198c8-8a0e-3b57-8171-dbd1ab6e2498",
                        "entry_id": "788443b2-9511-3df3-87f8-a335766be8f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, or being a form of verse, based on the number of syllables in a line rather than on the arrangement of accents or quantities."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
